      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027re right that with the current usage we should be able to do a mutable reference here. I ended up using take since I need it for malloc zone implementation, where I call things\nlike ```mem.alloc_in(heap, size)``` and the borrow checker does not like that. Figured I can save the future edit by just doing it this way now.",
